    "stall_speeds_provenance": {
      "title": "Stall Speeds",
      "conditions": "Power off, most forward center of gravity, 1600 lb",
      "note": "Figure 5-3, printed page 5-10, prints two blocks: most REARWARD and most FORWARD C.G. Only the most-forward block is carried, and the clip is set to that block alone. It is the conservative one (1 to 2 kt higher at every flap and bank setting except 40 deg flap, where the two agree), and it is the only one that can be carried unambiguously: the shared extractor reads its C.G. block labels from the PDF text layer, which on this scanned sheet is unusable, so a two-block extraction returns both blocks with cg null and no way to tell them apart. The cg field is therefore null on every row and the C.G. condition is stated here instead. KIAS values are approximate, per the handbook's own note.",
